**Read:** [Machine learning and materials informatics — Ramprasad and colleagues](../sources/Materials-Informatics-Ramprasad.lingua#r_6CKWYT91KQJRX7EWD6TK53VFRM), complete descriptor and application sections; [Data Evaluation: Theory and Practice for Materials Properties — Ronald G. Munro](../sources/Data-Evaluation-for-Materials-Properties-NIST.lingua#r_7N31EWH1JVE54EM3BRSQGYS04K), identity of the reported property; earlier state/history work.

A data representation decides what distinctions a model can learn. Composition alone cannot distinguish heat treatments of the same alloy; a structure descriptor may omit surfaces, defects or measurement conditions. If two physically different cases receive identical inputs, no deterministic predictor using only those inputs can separate their responses.

Choose invariance in relation to the output. Scalar energy should not change under a rigid rotation of an isolated configuration; a tensor response changes components with the coordinate frame. Erasing orientation can destroy the information needed for an anisotropic property. Units, normalization and missing-value handling are part of the method.

**Work:** Define descriptors for a structural and a functional material question. Construct a pair of cases your initial representation cannot distinguish, then decide whether additional state information is obtainable. Test relevant symmetry transformations. Explain why a descriptor suited to a bulk equilibrium property may be insufficient for fatigue, corrosion or a processed interface.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
